WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.800
Clip 1: In a portrait view, a G1 robot takes steps from the floor onto a padded incline. The robot is upright near the end of the excerpt. An overhead tether and an operator with its controller remain visible.

00:03.800 --> 00:05.800
Hard cut to Clip 2, a separate landscape recording. The robot stands beside a padded incline, attached to a gantry. An operator stands to the left.

00:05.800 --> 00:07.800
The robot takes steps forward onto the padded surface.

00:07.800 --> 00:09.800
The robot bends its torso and lowers a handheld tool toward the surface. The operator and attached safety tether remain visible.

00:09.800 --> 00:10.800
The robot begins to raise its torso before this selected excerpt ends.

00:10.800 --> 00:14.200
Hard cut to Clip 3, another laboratory recording. The robot steps forward and begins lowering its torso toward the padded surface.

00:14.200 --> 00:16.600
The robot bends deeply and brings its hand and tool close to the surface. This selected excerpt ends before later motion. All clips retain original speed, without sound; full trial outcomes are not shown.
